  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday morning through next Sunday)\nIssued at 153 PM EDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nOne final day of widespread heat index values exceeding 100 is \nexpected before temperatures ease to something a little more \nreasonable. A cold front (and I use the word 'cold' liberally) is \nexpected late Wednesday afternoon and into the overnight hours of \nThursday. A few areas in the southern part of the CWA may continue \nto see HI values as high as 100 through the week. Afternoon \nthunderstorms chances increase as a result, but as of right now \nthere is only a marginal chance for severe weather as the best \ndynamics remain off to the northeast. The front will filter in some \ndrier air, and while temps will remain in the upper 80s and lower \n90s it won't be nearly as humid.\n\nAfternoon thunderstorm activity will continue through the rest of \nthe week. As always, a few strong storms could be possible each \nafternoon. Gusty winds, frequent lightning and some localized flash \nflooding will be the main concerns to watch out for.\n\nWe continue to monitor the current tropical depression in the gulf, \nbut we agree with NHC's track and are unlikely to see significant \nimpacts as a result through the long term forecast period.",
